00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:35,000
Chaos Theory

413
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:35,000
Homeostasis

414
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,450
<i>Stupid Daru...</i>

415
00:02:34,450 --> 00:02:36,960
<i>Spreading our secrets to outsiders...</i>

416
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:36,960
Why?

417
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,130
Why must you take it that way?

418
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:40,210
I just wanted to...

419
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,670
No, that isn't what I meant!

420
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:43,590
I...

421
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:08,700
Wh-Wh-What?

422
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:09,910
I'm not crying!

423
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:12,030
It's not like I was crying, okay?

424
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:14,830
You were clearly crying...

425
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,500
Your eyes are still red.

426
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,620
No!

427
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,710
Something's in my eye...

428
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:22,540
What is this, an old soap opera?

429
00:03:23,090 --> 00:03:25,210
Anyway, I'm not crying.

430
00:03:25,210 --> 00:03:26,760
So no questions.

431
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,720
Got it?

432
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,390
I didn't say anything.

433
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,930
Shut up!

434
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:52,700
Christina...

435
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:53,450
Don't talk to me!

436
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:00,500
I'll only say this...

437
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,130
You're part of my life now.

438
00:04:03,130 --> 00:04:05,130
Any time you want to talk, I'll listen.

439
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:07,840
Okabe...

440
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:11,930
Just as planned, she fell for it!

441
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:16,390
Now I can use her for all the grunt work!

442
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:18,770
Hey.

443
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:23,400
Good work out there!

444
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:25,570
Feyris-chan!

445
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:27,440
Are you heading to Kyouma's?

446
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:30,150
Yeah, he wanted me to bring lunch.

447
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:35,660
Hey, have you seen the time machine, Mayushii?

448
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:36,950
Time...

449
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,370
Oh, Phone Microwave-san?

450
00:04:39,370 --> 00:04:40,710
Phone Microwave?

451
00:04:40,710 --> 00:04:46,840
There's this big spooky lightning, and it's kind of scary...

452
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:49,460
Wow!

453
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:51,920
It's like a time machine out of the movies.

454
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,720
Yeah...

455
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:58,810
But Mayushii doesn't really want him doing that stuff.

456
00:04:58,810 --> 00:05:00,020
Why?

457
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:06,150
It feels like Okarin is leaving me.

458
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,610
We will now begin our Roundâ

459
00:05:09,610 --> 00:05:11,150
Okarin! Okarin!

460
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:12,860
What?

461
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:14,280
Isn't this strange?

462
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:17,330
Mayushii says she isn't cosplaying.

463
00:05:17,330 --> 00:05:18,240
It isn't cosplay.

464
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,410
It's her school uniform.

465
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,700
I had school today.

466
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:25,630
It's a super-realistic portrayal of a school uniform.

467
00:05:25,630 --> 00:05:28,090
That's sexual harassment, and she doesn't have to accept it.

468
00:05:28,090 --> 00:05:30,250
Here's yours, Okarin!

469
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:31,210
Thanks.

470
00:05:31,210 --> 00:05:33,220
No, wait. I said we're having a Round Table!

471
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:37,140
You're the one who wanted me to bring lunch.

472
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,050
Don't mind him.

473
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,680
Obviously, it isn't anything important.

474
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:43,230
You can say that after you hear the discussion topic...

475
00:05:43,730 --> 00:05:45,940
Physical time travel!

476
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:51,610
Mayuri, is there still barley tea in the fridge?

477
00:05:51,610 --> 00:05:53,320
One second.

478
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,400
Realistic.

479
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,030
It's me!

480
00:05:57,030 --> 00:06:00,870
The Organization has initiated an operation to tear apart the lab.

481
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:02,950
The words of me, Hououin Kyouma,

482
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:05,000
fail to reach them!

483
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,500
Do they ever?

484
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:09,920
Then why are you ignoring my awesome topic?

485
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,800
Because it's impossible.

486
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:14,130
We can send messages to the past.

487
00:06:14,130 --> 00:06:15,090
It must be possible...

488
00:06:15,090 --> 00:06:15,760
It's not.

489
00:06:16,470 --> 00:06:19,220
We can send thirty-six bytes plus some extra.

490
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:20,970
Three messages, with six characters.

491
00:06:20,970 --> 00:06:22,520
No more.

492
00:06:22,970 --> 00:06:26,560
If you want to experiment, why not be the guinea pig?

493
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,810
That's if you don't mind ending up as a gel-Okarin.

494
00:06:29,810 --> 00:06:31,900
Gel-Okarin, huh?

495
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,070
That'd really hurt.

496
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:35,820
SERN's experiments prove the difficulties

497
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,530
inherent to physical time travel.

498
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:41,080
Even using the LHC, biggest in the world,

499
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,830
they've had no success.

500
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:44,580
We can't possibly do it with this equipment.

501
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:47,330
Then how do the messages get to the past?

502
00:06:47,330 --> 00:06:48,710
I don't know.

503
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:49,830
That's the problem.

504
00:06:50,330 --> 00:06:51,840
Like I said before,

505
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:54,130
SERN's trying to use the lifter-black hole combination

506
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:56,090
to achieve time travel.

507
00:06:56,590 --> 00:06:59,680
The Phone Microwave probably works on the same principle.

508
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:02,720
But the microwave doesn't have anything

509
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,310
to function as a lifter.

510
00:07:04,310 --> 00:07:05,390
So where is it?

511
00:07:05,390 --> 00:07:06,230
I don't know.

512
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:10,020
We're limited in the times we can send D-mail, too.

513
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:12,860
Currently, we can't be sure that this machine

514
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,360
really sends messages to the past.

515
00:07:15,070 --> 00:07:16,440
Before we continue,

516
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,490
we should deal with the issues before us first.

517
00:07:18,990 --> 00:07:19,910
Boring!

518
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:24,410
99.9% of science is boring.

519
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:26,750
If you call yourself a scientist...

520
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:28,210
I'm not a scientist!

521
00:07:28,210 --> 00:07:30,040
I'm a mad scientist!

522
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:33,960
Yo, I heard you like fail, so we put some fail in your fail, 
so you can facepalm while you facepalm.

523
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,250
Miss Makise...

524
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,970
You aren't a...

525
00:07:37,970 --> 00:07:38,840
Shut up!

526
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:39,800
Not another word!

527
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,220
Because that's impossible!

528
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,800
Get back on topic, already.

529
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:46,520
Continuing on to the reports.

530
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:48,020
How's the translation of

531
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:51,270
the SERN server documents going, Christina?

532
00:07:51,690 --> 00:07:53,230
AKA, 2channer!

533
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:55,440
I told you that's not true!

534
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,900
Then you sure know your memes.

535
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,030
I do not!

536
00:08:01,610 --> 00:08:03,910
Nothing to report.

537
00:08:03,910 --> 00:08:04,830
I see.

538
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:06,830
Continue your investigations...

539
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:07,620
2channer!

540
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:08,620
Stop calling me that!

541
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:10,750
Daru's up next. How's the hacking coming?

542
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:11,920
No change.

543
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:14,790
Probably, until I analyze the mysterious program

544
00:08:14,790 --> 00:08:17,340
on the other server, there'll be no change.

545
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:19,010
How's the IBN 5100 analysis going?

546
00:08:19,010 --> 00:08:21,220
Be great if I could do it.

547
00:08:22,010 --> 00:08:23,720
What do you mean?

548
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,100
Huh?

549
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:27,390
You haven't started the analysis?

550
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,730
How should I do that?

551
00:08:30,850 --> 00:08:33,190
Where's the IBN 5100?

552
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:35,230
How would I know?

553
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,150
It can't be...

554
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,700
Okarin, what's wrong?

555
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,950
Christina...

556
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:52,160
Did I, by any chance, not find the IBN 5100?

557
00:08:53,370 --> 00:08:57,550
You don't even know where it is.

558
00:09:01,970 --> 00:09:03,220
I see.

559
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:08,390
So if I decide to believe what you say, you found the IBN 5100.

560
00:09:08,390 --> 00:09:09,270
Yes.

561
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:11,730
I carried it back here with you.

562
00:09:11,730 --> 00:09:15,770
But you're the only one with any memory of that.

563
00:09:15,770 --> 00:09:18,820
The D-mails probably changed the past.

564
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:21,490
Changed the past...

565
00:09:21,490 --> 00:09:24,860
But we've only sent minor stuff.

566
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,910
The Butterfly Effect.

567
00:09:28,950 --> 00:09:31,120
Sending one message into the past

568
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,330
causes the world line to split.

569
00:09:33,330 --> 00:09:35,670
From a world where we didn't buy a Lotto-6 ticket

570
00:09:35,670 --> 00:09:36,880
to one where we did.

571
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:41,300
Little by little, this changes what was meant to happen.

572
00:09:42,210 --> 00:09:43,510
One change causes another,

573
00:09:43,510 --> 00:09:47,890
and they pile on top of one another.

574
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:52,270
It's one of the long-recognized risks of altering the past.

575
00:09:52,770 --> 00:09:55,690
Then where is the IBN 5100?

576
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:57,100
Let me ask this instead.

577
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:57,900
Where was it?

578
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:05,490
Yes, when I asked my dad, he said it used to be here, but...

579
00:10:06,950 --> 00:10:09,450
It's gone now.

580
00:10:09,870 --> 00:10:10,790
I see.

581
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,080
Well?

582
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:18,830
There was an IBN 5100 at Yanabayashi Shrine.

583
00:10:19,210 --> 00:10:21,090
But it's gone now.

584
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:24,050
No one knows when it was taken or by whom.

585
00:10:24,550 --> 00:10:26,180
A dead end, huh?

586
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:30,600
But it's strange to donate a PC to a shrine.

587
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,770
I wonder who'd have done that.

588
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:41,820
Feyris-chan?

589
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:42,570
What's up?

590
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:46,450
Here's the list I wrote of ten questions

591
00:10:46,450 --> 00:10:47,990
to ask the maids, at the next event.

592
00:10:47,990 --> 00:10:49,120
Let me see...

593
00:10:50,410 --> 00:10:54,540
"If you could go back and redo one thing from your past, what would it be?"

594
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:57,080
What would you do, Feyris-chan?

595
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:00,250
Let me think...

596
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,800
Feyris... doesn't look back at her past! Let's go.

597
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,840
It's the task of the cat-eared maid,

598
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:09,180
who brings everyone happiness, to forge ahead!

599
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:13,560
Oh, my phone!

600
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:15,270
Hi, this is Feyris.

601
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:16,980
Kyouma.

602
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:18,390
A PC?

603
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:20,900
An IBN 5100.

604
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:24,320
Did your family give it to Yanabayashi Shrine?

605
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:27,030
I don't really remember...

606
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:31,490
But you're right. My dad did have a lot of old PCs.

607
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,330
Kyouma...

608
00:11:36,750 --> 00:11:39,290
Is this related to the time machine

609
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:41,250
you were talking about?

610
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:46,630
Look, look!

611
00:11:46,630 --> 00:11:47,760
It's an Upa!

612
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:49,090
A metal Upa!

613
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:53,390
Do you still want a metal Upa?

614
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:54,600
Still?

615
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,730
How long are you going to stand there, staring at it?

616
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:03,360
Wait!

617
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,690
Daru-kun!

618
00:12:04,690 --> 00:12:06,070
Here I am!

619
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,780
What are you buying?

620
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:15,160
I found a limited-edition that had sold out before I could buy it!

621
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,790
You might say,

622
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:19,870
"This encounter was the choice of Steins Gate!"

623
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:21,000
Don't use it for stuff like this!

624
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:24,500
Anyway, why are you two following me?

625
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,840
You could've stayed back at the lab, with the assistant.

626
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,960
Once I heard you were going to Feyris-tan's place,

627
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:31,220
I had to come along!

628
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:33,220
I wanted to go and play, too!

629
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:37,310
Why did Feyris tell me to come to her house?

630
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:38,520
It's Kirari-chan!

631
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,810
Mayuri, wait...

632
00:12:40,850 --> 00:12:42,270
Jeez...

633
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,400
The IBN 5100.

634
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:55,120
Shining Finger!

635
00:12:58,740 --> 00:12:59,910
Wait! Hey!

636
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:05,830
Shining...

637
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:06,710
Moeka!

638
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:07,840
Kiryuu Moeka!

639
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,940
Why?

640
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:31,150
FB said it was there!

641
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:35,700
Okabe-kun...

642
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:37,660
Back there, you mentioned the IBN 5100...

643
00:13:38,910 --> 00:13:41,950
Do you know... where it is?

644
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:46,210
You don't know, either?

645
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,630
I don't...

646
00:13:57,390 --> 00:13:58,890
Okarin!

647
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,060
Moeka-san?

648
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:02,140
Yeah.

649
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:03,270
Okabe...

650
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:06,940
Moeka-san's so pretty and stylish.

651
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:09,650
I'm sure she'd make a great cosplayer.

652
00:14:12,530 --> 00:14:16,160
Mayuri, you know Shining Finger?

653
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,450
I do!

654
00:14:18,450 --> 00:14:19,490
How?

655
00:14:19,490 --> 00:14:20,830
How do you know her?

656
00:14:20,830 --> 00:14:23,830
You brought her to the lab!

657
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:27,710
<i>After Moeka sent her D-mail,</i>

658
00:14:28,330 --> 00:14:30,670
<i>she disappeared from everyone's memory.</i>

659
00:14:31,590 --> 00:14:35,010
<i>And then, after Ruka sent his D-mail,</i>

660
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:37,550
<i>they knew her again.</i>

661
00:14:39,090 --> 00:14:41,640
<i>Little by little, the world changes,</i>

662
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:44,060
<i>each time the D-mail changes the past?</i>

663
00:14:58,910 --> 00:15:01,160
Is this really the place?

664
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,580
I'm sure of it.

665
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:06,210
Seems it's on the top floor.

666
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:16,510
The mistress will be here soon.

667
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:17,970
Just one moment.

668
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:26,020
Butler cafÃ©s aren't my thing.

669
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:27,430
A real butler!

670
00:15:27,430 --> 00:15:29,480
I've never seen one before.

671
00:15:32,110 --> 00:15:32,940
Look!

672
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,320
The people all look like ants!

673
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,400
I love it!

674
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:38,200
Okarin...

675
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,910
Thought he'd say that!

676
00:15:39,910 --> 00:15:41,240
Sorry for the wait.

677
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:42,740
Feyris-chan!

678
00:15:43,950 --> 00:15:46,540
Now it's Feyris-tan wearing her normal clothes!

679
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:48,830
What luck!

680
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:51,920
Feyris Nyan Nyan!

681
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:56,420
It seems I must question your true identity!

682
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:58,760
Feyris is...

683
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:00,760
...Feyris-nyan!

684
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:02,050
Stop fooling around!

685
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:05,350
If you refuse to explain, then I'm leaving!

686
00:16:05,350 --> 00:16:07,270
Oh, fine.

687
00:16:09,230 --> 00:16:13,650
Feyris's family owns all the land around here!

688
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:16,570
Then Akiba is...

689
00:16:16,570 --> 00:16:18,110
That's right.

690
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,110
What about Akiba now?

691
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:21,990
It's Feyris's real name.

692
00:16:21,990 --> 00:16:23,740
Akiha Rumiho-chan!

693
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:26,080
I didn't hear that!

694
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:28,410
Feyris-tan's real name is Feyris-tan!

695
00:16:28,830 --> 00:16:30,960
A sad attempt to escape reality.

696
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:33,170
By the way, Feyris was the one

697
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:36,300
who asked to bring moe culture to Akiba.

698
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:37,250
No way!

699
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:40,300
And she works as an angel at May Queen,

700
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,720
to further spread moe culture!

701
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,260
How splendid!

702
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:47,560
And my eyes are also splendid, 
for recognizing her before anyone else!

703
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:52,310
But, but... Keep it a secret, okay?

704
00:16:52,310 --> 00:16:53,940
I want you to treat me

705
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:55,690
with Feyris-love, just like always!

706
00:16:55,690 --> 00:16:57,860
I will! Totally!

707
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:59,230
Thank you, nyan-nyan!

708
00:16:59,230 --> 00:17:00,530
No nyan-nyan!

709
00:17:00,530 --> 00:17:03,160
Anyway, what about the IBN 5100?

710
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,450
Oh, that?

711
00:17:05,450 --> 00:17:10,160
But before that, I have a simple request...

712
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,210
You want to arrange a trade?

713
00:17:12,210 --> 00:17:14,120
It's nothing difficult.

714
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:17,590
I only want you to let me use the D-mail. Just once.

715
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,050
Sure!

716
00:17:20,050 --> 00:17:21,380
Use it as often as you want!

717
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:24,640
Wait! The D-mail is absolutely off-limits to outsiders...

718
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:28,350
Then why not make Feyris-chan a lab member, too?

719
00:17:28,350 --> 00:17:29,890
Wait! Wait!

720
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:33,190
Sending more messages to the past would beâ

721
00:17:33,190 --> 00:17:37,020
You're the one who sent the Lotto-6 number back, 
to try and make money!

722
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,610
And you can't send one for Feyris-tan?

723
00:17:38,610 --> 00:17:40,070
Just once!

724
00:17:40,070 --> 00:17:41,990
No, that's not it...

725
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:45,450
<i>But if I stop now,</i>

726
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:48,450
<i>there's no guarantee that the IBN 5100 will return.</i>

727
00:17:49,450 --> 00:17:51,910
<i>If this becomes any kind of clue...</i>

728
00:17:54,250 --> 00:17:55,080
Very well.

729
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:57,630
But just as Mayuri said,

730
00:17:57,630 --> 00:17:59,290
you'll have to become a lab member.

731
00:17:59,290 --> 00:18:02,880
You are now Lab Member 007, Akiha Ruâ

732
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,880
I-I-I can't hear you!

733
00:18:08,430 --> 00:18:09,600
It's done.

